      {
        "id": "95e6d9fd-5431-40fa-9e1f-99b4cfb6db7e",
        "title": "Inspiration",
        "body": "My inspiration comes from several scenes in Stephen Chow’s films.<br><br>The first reference is the depiction of the <span style=\"background-color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">mermaid</span>’s appearance in <em>The Mermaid</em>. <br>To make the character easier to design and animate in Unreal Engine, I decided to combine several visual elements from different interpretations of mermaids and create a standing mermaid character with a fish head and a humanoid body. <br><br>The second reference is the “<span style=\"background-color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Strange Gun</span>” from <em>From Beijing with Love</em>. This weapon has two firing ports at the front and back, and bullets are randomly fired from either side.",
        "titleColor": "#10110d",
        "bodyColor": "#ff4a00",
        "titleBold": true,
        "bodyBold": false,
        "titleSize": 80,
        "bodySize": 28,
