      {
        "id": "3594a380-1836-4002-a28a-82c8df97642a",
        "title": "Core Game Mechanics",
        "body": "The player controls a fish-headed humanoid character who uses the “Strange Gun” to <span style=\"background-color: rgb(16, 17, 13);\">attack approaching enemies</span> in <span style=\"background-color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">first person mode</span>.<br><br>When bullets hit enemies, they can either reduce the enemies’ health or kill them instantly. (The final effect will be adjusted according to the number of enemies and their movement speed during further development). <br>If the bullets hit the player themselves, their entire health bar will be emptied in one shot. <br>The player needs to <span style=\"background-color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">press the space key</span> to <span style=\"background-color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">switch</span> the front and back <span style=\"background-color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">directions</span> of the gun in order to avoid being hit by their own bullets.",
        "titleColor": "#cfff00",
        "bodyColor": "#ffffff",
        "titleBold": true,
        "bodyBold": false,
        "titleSize": 80,
        "bodySize": 28,
        "layout": 0,
        "bg": "#ff4a00",
        "stageWidth": 100,
        "stageHeight": 500,
