      {
        "id": "653873e5-e8b2-4ea0-aec7-5a69e0c49ee6",
        "title": "<span style=\"color: rgb(247, 247, 247);\">Core Game Mechanics</span>",
        "body": "Random <span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 74, 0);\">signposts</span> will rise  in the environment. These signposts contain light indicators that provide <span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 72, 0);\">hints about the firing direction</span> of the next several bullets. <br>When bullets are fired in direction A, the corresponding lights will turn on; when bullets are fired in direction B, the lights will remain off.<br>The <span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 72, 0);\">number of lights</span> on the signpost will gradually <span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 72, 0);\">increase</span>, starting from four lights and eventually reaching ten lights. (This will be adjusted based on the actual difficulty of implementation and the overall game balance).<br><br><br>Accordingly, the player’s ability to predict bullet directions will progress from remembering the next four shots to <span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 74, 0);\">remembering</span> the next ten shots. ",
